{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f1f519c16bc795c83c94655c1012fb77e77c86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-2,1)--(2,1)--(2,-1)--(-2,-1)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(0,-1)--(-2,-1)--(-2,0)--cycle); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(0,0),E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-2,1),W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(2,1),E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (2,-1),E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-2,-1),WSW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(-2,0),W); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(0,-1),S); //Credit to TheMaskedMagician for the diagram [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p>If rectangle ABCD has area 72 square meters and E and G are the midpoints of sides AD and CD, respectively, then the area of rectangle DEFG in square meters is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/37687b3d841a7d2c7cb27f38a962b4fafa0763e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }8\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }9\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }12\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }18\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"380\" height=\"17\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>Since the dimensions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> are half of the dimensions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b01aeb188758282b484f800e4089df825baf1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"38\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bba8c59b0ba18eec261350adf78769d6e9b7528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot72 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems<